      "t": "2026-11-19T00:00:01Z",
      "text": "Gaza's health ministry reports that two people were killed by recent Israeli attacks, and two others died from their wounds over the past day.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:2026-11-19:7"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-19T00:00:08Z",
      "text": "A UN report from November 2026 accused Israel of committing war crimes and crimes against humanity in the occupied West Bank, including extermination, torture, and sexual assault.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:rev:1386596237:403"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-19T00:00:15Z",
      "text": "The Gaza war is an armed conflict in the Gaza Strip and Israel, fought as part of the unresolved Israeli–Palestinian and Gaza–Israel conflicts.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:rev:1386596237:0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-19T00:00:25Z",
      "text": "On the map, the reports place the story in the Gaza Strip.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:2026-11-19:7"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-19T00:00:33Z",
      "text": "The reports also name the Levant.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:2026-11-19:7"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-19T00:00:42Z",
      "text": "The story is reported by Al Jazeera.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:2026-11-19:7"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-19T00:00:50Z",
      "text": "Al Jazeera headlined it: “Gaza Syndrome: Why Israeli soldiers’ trauma erases Palestinian victims.”",
      "cites": [
        "news:aljazeera:08c4ee3f1046"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-19T00:00:56Z",
      "text": "The Guardian headlined it: “Israeli tanks cross ‘yellow line’ boundary into Hamas-controlled central Gaza.”",
      "cites": [
